  "result": "I've found the matching tickets and am writing up the answer.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47609\", \"PowerToys#48512\", \"PowerToys#35312\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. New+ doesn't show in the classic context menu when the HKCU\\\\Software\\\\Classes\\\\CLSID\\\\{86ca1aa0-34aa-4e8b-a509-50c905bae2a2} key is present. The Explorer handler gets loaded but adds no entry on a folder background. I found no fix in the archive, and #48512 is still a feature request for classic-menu support. The workaround reported in #35312 and #35210 is to enable Developer Mode, turn New+ off, run Remove-AppxPackage on the Microsoft.PowerToys.NewPlusContextMenu package, then turn New+ back on and restart explorer.exe. It didn't work for the reporter of #48512, though. Reboots or hibernating also helped some users, and others reported success after a full uninstall and reinstall. The reliable option for now is to delete the registry key (reg.exe delete \\\"HKCU\\\\Software\\\\Classes\\\\CLSID\\\\{86ca1aa0-34aa-4e8b-a509-50c905bae2a2}\\\" /f) and restart Explorer to get the Windows 11 menu back. You can also add your report and bug-report zip to #47609 or #48512.\"}",
